Figure S12. Spatial variation in estimated effective diversity and migration. (a) Effective diversity q and (b) effective migration m from the archived 700-deme EEMS analysis of 217 individuals and 38,124 SNPs. Colors show posterior means of relative log10 rates, with separate scales for q and m; blue and orange indicate relatively higher and lower values, respectively. Black points indicate sampling locations. The archived run used 2,000,000 iterations, including 1,000,000 burn-in iterations, and retained 100 draws at intervals of 10,000 iterations (seed 123). Surfaces are descriptive model summaries and do not quantify contemporary dispersal rates, future movement or genetic rescue. Only one chain for this grid was recovered, so independent-chain convergence has not been demonstrated.

Source check: both submitted maps visually agree with the archived700-deme q/m maps. Exact historical plotting options remain unavailable; q/m labels follow saved object names and source documentation.
